WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
 The people that are on
your team, the people that

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.610
are in your group,
your family, whoever.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.470
You're coaching, you
might not even know it,

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.840
but you're coaching.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.598
For you, as a team
leader, you're

00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:13.140
only going to be
able to do it if you

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.000
can build great relationships.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.210
We've won 11 national
championships in the last 25

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:18.960
years.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.480
I won two gold medals
at the Olympics

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.700
coaching the US national team.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.950
Teams are teams, no
matter what situation.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.980
It's a group of people
trying to come together

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.950
to do something that they
can't do individually.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.950
Some of the things that
you're going to learn

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.860
are: how to get the best
people on your team--

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.740
that's number one, that's
key-- how to work with them so

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.200
that you can raise
their level from where

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.570
they are, to where
they hope to be,

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.100
to where you need them to be.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.900
It's the same in sports, and
it's the same in business,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.300
and it's the same in life.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.440
How do we build those
championship teams?

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.680
How do we train those
incredible players?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.980
I go by the old-fashioned
Catholic Italian way.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.620
You just make them feel guilty.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.370
So you ask them, flat-out,
"is this the best you got?"

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.690
and invariably, they'll
say, "no, I got more."

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:08.190
All right.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:08.730
Let's go.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.530
Let's see it.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.590
One of the biggest attributes
that resilient leaders

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.232
have, is the ability to listen,
listen more than you talk,

00:01:18.232 --> 00:01:19.690
because when I got
to this country,

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.060
I didn't speak English.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.720
So you're kind of
forced to grow up fast.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.910
Pay attention and
learn by watching,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.740
and learn by listening.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.260
I truly believe
there's always pressure

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.450
when you're trying to
accomplish something that's

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.580
meaningful and rewarding;
and because of the pressure

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.930
and because you perform and
you handle it a certain way,

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.780
you've just grown as a person.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.590
You've just become something
more than what you were before.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:50.880
Winning teams, understand that
the pursuit of winning never

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.660
ends.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.420
Winning a game, is
really teaching you

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.520
how to win at life.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.190
Any group can benefit
from the strategies

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.710
we're going to talk about;
and you, as a leader,

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.500
can help them reach
their potential.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.190
I'm Geno Auriemma, and
this is MasterClass.

